# Read-only `ha` CLI allow-list for Claude jobs (design §4.5, layer 2).
#
# Format: one command per line, tokens separated by single spaces, starting with `ha`.
# A trailing ` *` means the command accepts further arguments (flags such as --lines);
# without it the rule must name the command exactly. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# A job's `Bash(ha …)` rule is valid only if its tokens prefix-match one of these lines.
# Every mutating verb (restart, update, rebuild, options, reboot, restore, …) is absent by
# construction, and the per-run token broker has no route for them either.
#
# `logs` verbs are effectively `--lines`/`-n` only: the job's `ha` wrapper strips
# -f/--follow and -b/--boot before exec (a follow would block until the job timeout),
# and the validator rejects any rule that names those flags.
#
# CLI 5.x spells add-ons `ha apps …`; `ha addons …` is a deprecated alias. Both are accepted.

ha core check
ha core info
ha core stats
ha core logs *
ha supervisor info
ha supervisor stats
ha supervisor logs *
ha resolution info
ha os info
ha host info
ha host logs *
ha addons
ha addons info *
ha apps
ha apps info *
ha backups
ha backups info *
